From 52b77a67d5ec8fd5c8e0fb555d793265e9ea5af9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hans Bihs <hans.bihs@ntnu.no>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 00:02:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/13] ghostcell: one message for gcparax + gcparacox, no
 periodic exchange without periodic neighbours

start1..4 exchanged the partition ghost cells (gcparax) and then the corner
cells (gcparacox) in two neighbour collectives, both with the field values
before the boundary ghost cells are set. gcparax_co packs both into one
message (paraco cells after the gcpara cells, same receive order), so the
result is the same with one collective less. The send/recv buffers already
had room for both (gcx_ini).

gcperiodicx exchanged the periodic partition faces in every start*, also
when no rank has periodic partition neighbours (empty lists, but still a
collective). gcx_ini now checks once (globalisum) and gcperiodicx returns
when there is none; the decision is the same on all ranks.

3D dam break with obstacle (4 ranks): neighbour collectives per time step
538 -> 298. Regression 34/34 and validation 29/29 bitwise identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0114EoYH2J5n8x9czzdi2yNp
