Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 00:02:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/13] time step, probes, gauges: one reduction instead of one
 per value

ietimestep / etimestep / fixtimestep reduced u, v, w, F, G, H, fb, nu,
k, eps, p max/min one MPI_Allreduce each (fbmax twice), interleaved with
the loops. Now all local maxima first, then one MPI_Allreduce (MAX, the
pressure minimum as max of -p). probe_point (P 61) reduced 7 values per
probe, print_wsf (P 51) one per gauge: now one reduction for all.

3D dam break with obstacle (4 ranks): MPI_Allreduce per step 366 -> 347
(the rest is the pressure solver and BiCGStab). Bitwise identical,
also the screen output.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0114EoYH2J5n8x9czzdi2yNp
