From 550a67349e2644e395569206f6833fab4a6247fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hans Bihs <hans.bihs@ntnu.no>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 00:02:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/13] time step: CFL minimum over all ranks

ietimestep and etimestep computed the CFL limit cu (and cb for the
floating-body time step) as the minimum over the cells of each rank and
then broadcast rank 0's value (timesync): the time step came from rank 0's
cells only. On stretched grids, or with the smallest cells on another
rank, the CFL number was exceeded there. Now the minimum over all ranks
(one MPI_Allreduce for cu and cb in ietimestep).

etimestep::ini used cu uninitialised; now 1e10 as in start.

Results change in MPI runs only: on uniform grids by round-off (DXN from
coordinate differences differ in the last bit): the 3D MPI regression
cases are 'close' (1e-13 .. 1e-5 rel.).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0114EoYH2J5n8x9czzdi2yNp
