Subject: [PATCH 06/13] momentum forcing: rebuild the flags only when the
 geometry changed

solid_forcing_flag_update, gcdf_update and gcb_velflagio rebuilt all flag
arrays and gcdf lists in every RK stage (about 10 passes over the grid and
12 halo exchanges of int arrays per stage), also for fixed geometry. They
depend on the geometry only through sign tests of solid, topo and fb
(against 0 and, for G 5, against psi = -X41 dx). ghostcell::geometry_changed
keeps these per cell (2 bytes) and returns true if any changed on any rank
(one MPI_Allreduce); the rebuild runs only then (always on the first call;
6DOF, sediment and the solid modules still rebuild themselves).

3D dam break with obstacle (4 ranks): neighbour collectives per step
298 -> 244 (with the previous commit). Bitwise identical (regression
34/34, validation 30/30).

